course: dictionary
lesson: 566
title: Auntie: more than family
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one fits. Auntie is a friendly, informal word for your mum's or dad's sister, or your uncle's wife. «Auntie Sue is coming to tea» is a family name for a relative.
explain: Now read the clues in this sentence: «Mashallah, so big now!» Hamid is at a wedding with 300 guests and about 20 aunties pinch his cheeks. Not all of them are his relatives, and the clue is that they are fond of him. In many families, auntie is a kind name for any older woman who is a friend of the family.
explain: Some languages use auntie as a title that reaches outside the family. «Any woman about your mum's age is āyí (auntie).» Here āyí is a respectful way to speak to a woman, like calling her auntie. A dictionary can confirm a meaning when the clues are not enough.
fact: Auntie means the sister of your mum or dad, or the wife of your uncle.
fact: Auntie is friendly and informal; aunt is the word used in family trees.
fact: In many communities, children call older women auntie as a sign of respect.
fact: Auntie can also be spelt aunty.
fact: «Hóngbāo» means red envelopes with money inside, given at New Year.
exercise: In «Auntie Sue is coming to tea», what does auntie mean? | *A friendly name for a relative, such as your mum's sister | A school teacher | A kind of cake
exercise: «At New Year Lín's aunties hand out hóngbāo.» What is a hóngbāo? | *A red envelope with money inside | Red sweets | A holiday card | A type of lantern
exercise: Hamid's cheeks were pinched by about 20 aunties. What does this tell you about them? | They are angry with him | They are his teachers | They are all his cousins | *They love him, even if it is very squeezy love
test: «Mia's cousin flips the Monopoly board, so the aunties ban Monopoly at Christmas.» Why do the aunties ban Monopoly? | Because the board is new | Because it is raining | *Because the cousin flipped the board across the room | Because they love playing it too much
test: In many communities, children call older women auntie to show what? | *Respect | Boredom | Sleepiness | Anger
exam: In «three aunties asked where it was from», what does auntie mean? | *Older women, or family friends who are women | A kind of jacket | A sort of suit | A type of shop
